WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.859 --> 00:00:10.929
Zirconium is a metal and I actually have here
a vodka glass made out of zirconium, which

00:00:10.929 --> 00:00:14.490
was given to me by a Russian scientist some
years ago.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:18.190
So here is a sample of zirconium foil. It
is a really quite beautiful element; it is

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:20.450
really quite hard, really tough metal.

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:27.860
Now the reason why zirconium was being manufactured
by this particular guy is because it is used

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:33.570
as the coating, or the so called cladding,
for the fuel rods in nuclear reactors.

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:40.460
Very useful for making tools and cutting devices:
very, very tough. Gosh, that’s hard!

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:50.149
But zirconium also has a whole series of uses.
The oxide of zirconium, zirconia, is used

00:00:50.149 --> 00:00:53.170
sometimes as materials to support catalysts.

